# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trivy suppressions.
#
# Each entry is a deliberate decision with a reason, not a way to make a badge
# green. Vulnerabilities are NOT suppressed here -- they are fixed, or
# reported as unfixable in SECURITY.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# DS-0002: "Last USER command in Dockerfile should not be 'root'".
#
# The same finding hadolint reports as DL3002, and the same answer: PHP-FPM's
# master process needs root to create the pool listener and to populate the
# html volume on first start, then drops to www-data for every worker. An
# image forced to a non-root USER does not start.
#
# The compensating controls are real and asserted rather than claimed:
#   - the smoke suite verifies the WORKERS run as www-data in the running
#     container, which is the fact this rule is a proxy for
#   - compose.prod.yml sets cap_drop: ALL, adding back only SETUID, SETGID,
#     CHOWN and DAC_OVERRIDE
#   - no-new-privileges is set on every service and asserted by a test
#   - the nginx vhost prevents uploaded files being executed as PHP
#
# See docs/adr/001-container-strategy.md.
DS-0002
